add vite.onfig.js
base: "/samuel-portfolio",

Add to package.json
"homepage": "https://<your-username>.github.io/<repository-name>/",

Install
npm install gh-pages

Add to package.json
"preeploy":"npm run build",
"deploy":"gh-pages -d dist",

git init
git add .

git commit -m "first commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin git@github.com:Onayemi/samuel-portfolio.git
git push -u origin main

npm run deploy

# If there is error in push

git fetch origin
git pull origin main --rebase
git push origin main

Private: samuel-portfolio.git
public: samuel-pf.git

# To push to public repository and protect privates

git remote add public https://github.com/onayemi/samuel-pf.git

npm run build
npx gh-pages -d dist -r public

STEP 7 — Enable GitHub Pages on the Public Repo
In the public repo (samuel-portfolio):
Go to Settings → Pages
Source:
Branch: gh-pages
Folder: / (root)
Save

After 1–2 minutes, your site will be live at:
👉 https://onayemi.github.io/samuel-portfolio/

For Public:
upload the dist file to pblic repo

